Build class for free.
 
No useless theory.
No long videos.
 
Here is the prompt list:
==========================
1/ The 80/20 Learning Plan
==========================
Use this to focus only on the concepts that create the biggest results and skip everything else.
 
Prompt: I am learning [skill] for [goal].
 Baseline: [what you know].
 Apply the 80/20 rule to map the 20% of core concepts driving 80% of results.
 Create a 30-day roadmap in a table: Day, Topic, Why it matters, 1 practical exercise, and 1 strict checkpoint to prove mastery. Strip all fluff.
========================== 
2/ The Mental Model Guide
========================== 
Use this to understand difficult topics through practical examples.
 
Prompt: Teach me [topic].
 Layer 1: Simple analogy.
 Layer 2: The exact mental model.
 Layer 3: How a senior pro uses it in high-stakes scenarios.
 Layer 4: Common edge cases.
 Do not ask if I understand. Ask 1 difficult scenario-based question to force me to apply it.
========================== 
3/ The Project Planner
==========================
Use this to turn what you learn into real projects, one step at a time.
 
Prompt: I am learning [skill]. Generate 3 progressive projects (Beginner to Advanced).
 Include: The real-world problem solved, core concepts tested, strict constraints, exact execution steps, and a debugging guide detailing the top 3 errors I will make.
========================== 
4/ The Concept Breakdown
========================== 
Use this whenever you get stuck and need to understand exactly where you're going wrong.
 
Prompt: I am deeply stuck on: [paste concept]. Break it down for a beginner. 
Diagnose the exact logical leap I am missing. 
Provide 1 correct example, 1 counter-example showing what it is NOT, and 1 highly focused micro-exercise to test my brain.
========================== 
5/ The Active Recall System
========================== 
Use this to move important information into long-term memory.
 
Prompt: Build a high-intensity study pack for [topic]. 
Give me the 5 most crucial principles, 10 fill-in-the-blank statements for easily forgotten details, 5 critical-thinking scenario questions, and a strict 7-day spaced repetition schedule.
========================== 
6/ The Feynman Knowledge Check
========================== 
Use this to test what you know and uncover the gaps you have missed.
 
Prompt: Audit my explanation of [topic]: [insert text]. Act as a strict examiner. Find jargon used as a crutch. Expose my logical gaps. 
Tell me where my logic falls apart. Rewrite it to be 50% shorter and much punchier.

